WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.167
-Donald Trump and Ron DeSantis
are competing with each other

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.834
to see who can be more extreme
on culture war nonsense

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.601
in their appeals
to the MAGA base

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:11.400
with DeSantis going so far
as to ban books in schools

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.467
and give out tax breaks
for gas stoves,

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:14.834
and Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:16.868
claimed at a committee
hearing that elementary schools

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:19.033
are spending billions of dollars
on critical race theory.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.767
For more on this,
it's time for a closer look.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.968
A central thing
that Donald Trump revealed

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:28.267
about the modern
Republican Party

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.634
is they don't have
a coherent worldview or agenda.

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:32.267
They're completely
directionless.

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:33.734
They're basically Roombas

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.000
when they bump into something
they don't understand,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.734
they just head
the opposite way.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:41.133
You can see that any time
Trump opens his mouth,

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.200
he doesn't talk about
policies or issues.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.901
He talks about manufactured
right-wing grievances

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.400
he heard about on Fox News.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.234
Here's one example from his
recent campaign kickoff that,

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:53.000
as far as I can tell,
makes no sense whatsoever.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.467
-Every day for the United States
is always April Fools'' Day.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.601
This just occurred
to me yesterday,

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.934
because I see what's happening.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:03.067
I say, "What's going on?

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.634
What's happening? What's wrong?"

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.868
It's like April Fools'', right?

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:09.801
We have open borders
when they should be closed.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.167
April Fools'' Day, right?

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:15.200
We have prisoners and people
from mental institutions

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.300
and terrorists being dumped
into our country

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.934
when they should
not be accepted.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.300
April Fools'', right?

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.968
We have people in the midst
of the greatest crime wave

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.667
in the history
that want to defund our police.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:28.434
This is again, April Fools''.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:33.467
We have Antifa and BLM
who hate our country

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:35.467
and burn down our cities,

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.434
and they're totally protected
by law enforcement.

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:41.367
And yet they put
American patriots in jail.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.734
What's going on there?

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:46.133
That's all April 1st,
April 1st, April Fools'' Day.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.467
-I know this goes
without saying.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.501
Those are all really bad
April Fools'' pranks.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:56.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.501
Every day is April Fools' Day.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.567
Sounds like he's pitching
a sequel to "Groundhog Day".

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:00.801
[ Imitating Trump ] All right,
so get this --

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:03.667
I play a local sports anchor
who gets stranded

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:07.467
in a small town
called Palm Beach, Florida.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:09.701
And every day I wake up
and the alarm goes off,

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.801
and the same song plays --
"Wake Me Up Before You Go-Go"

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:15.334
by Wham! -- so, we'll
have to pay to license that,

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.634
or if it's too expensive,
I'll just record the sound

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.834
like "Get Me Out of Bed
Before You Leave-Leave".

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.467
There you go, that part's done.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.601
And then in the movie,
I realize it's the same day

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:25.868
all over again --
April Fools' Day,

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:26.968
April Fools' Day.

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:28.734
But because it's always
April Fools' Day,

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.834
I can't be sure
if it's the same day

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:34.200
or if it's a prank to make me
think it's the same day,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.267
and so I learn nothing and drive
off a cliff with a groundhog.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.767
[ Normal voice ] That's right,
every day is April Fools' Day.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.400
And honestly, I don't know
why he's complaining,

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.968
because he's exactly
the kind of dickhead

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:47.901
who loves April Fools' Day.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.968
A holiday where I lie to people

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.167
and then make fun of them
when they believe me?

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.734
I'm in!

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.033
Trump is in a competition

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.067
with his likely main rival
for the GOP nomination,

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.167
