which clearly flustered
the witness.

00:10:29.133 --> 00:10:31.167
But pay attention
to the amount of money

00:10:31.167 --> 00:10:34.834
she claims one school
received to promote CRT.

00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:37.367
-Mr. Dodaro, can you tell me

00:10:37.367 --> 00:10:41.534
how much -- how much
COVID cash went to CRT?

00:10:41.534 --> 00:10:42.868
-CRT?

00:10:42.868 --> 00:10:45.501
-Critical race theory
in education.

00:10:45.501 --> 00:10:46.767
-No, I do not know that.

00:10:46.767 --> 00:10:49.601
But I do know
that there's provisions

00:10:49.601 --> 00:10:53.300
that the federal funds
generally are not used --

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.334
are supposed to be used
for curriculum.

00:10:55.334 --> 00:10:56.334
-Oh.

00:10:56.334 --> 00:10:57.534
-That's a state --
-Oh, Mr. Dodaro,

00:10:57.534 --> 00:10:58.767
I have to tell you in Illinois

00:10:58.767 --> 00:11:02.000
that they received $5.1 billion

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.200
at an elementary school there,

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:07.167
that used it
for equity and diversity.

00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:10.801
-If that's true, which it's not,
I would think the problem

00:11:10.801 --> 00:11:14.133
would be less CRT and more
that one elementary school

00:11:14.133 --> 00:11:17.934
got $5.1 billion.

00:11:17.934 --> 00:11:21.300
She really said one school
got $5.1 billion.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.901
If that were true, other schools
would be so jealous.

00:11:23.901 --> 00:11:26.801
"We had to hold a bake sale
for new soccer jerseys."

00:11:26.801 --> 00:11:30.200
"We just financed
the last two 'Avatar' movies."

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.267
[ Laughter ]

00:11:32.267 --> 00:11:35.734
Which, by the way,
movies which I'm guessing

00:11:35.734 --> 00:11:37.501
Greene also thinks are real.

00:11:37.501 --> 00:11:39.300
"The deep state doesn't want
you to know

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:44.033
that all those people turn blue
from the COVID vaccine,

00:11:44.033 --> 00:11:46.868
and they're 3D now!"

00:11:46.868 --> 00:11:49.367
So that's who the GOP thinks
should be able

00:11:49.367 --> 00:11:50.367
to serve on committees.

00:11:50.367 --> 00:11:51.767
Meanwhile, today,
they voted to kick

00:11:51.767 --> 00:11:53.701
Minnesota Congresswoman
Ilhan Omar,

00:11:53.701 --> 00:11:56.767
a refugee and one of the only
two Muslim women in the House

00:11:56.767 --> 00:11:58.300
off the
Foreign Affairs Committee

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.267
for the simple reason
that they don't like her

00:12:00.267 --> 00:12:01.534
or her point of view.

00:12:01.534 --> 00:12:03.434
And by the way, that's not just
me saying that,

00:12:03.434 --> 00:12:05.901
even Matt Gaetz,
one of the Trumpiest members

00:12:05.901 --> 00:12:08.467
of the GOP, a guy who tried
to overturn the 2020 election

00:12:08.467 --> 00:12:10.334
and lied about
the January 6th insurrection,

00:12:10.334 --> 00:12:11.767
admitted as much this week.

00:12:11.767 --> 00:12:13.834
-The reason I think
a lot of Republicans

00:12:13.834 --> 00:12:16.868
want to kick Ilhan Omar off of
the Foreign Affairs Committee

00:12:16.868 --> 00:12:19.300
is because they don't like
what she has to say.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.067
-You know how [Bleep] up
something has to be

00:12:21.067 --> 00:12:22.534
for me to agree with Matt Gaetz?

00:12:22.534 --> 00:12:25.901
The only other thing
we see eye to eye on

00:12:25.901 --> 00:12:27.701
are the benefits
of large foreheads.

00:12:27.701 --> 00:12:32.667
We see eye to eye,
forehead to forehead.

00:12:34.901 --> 00:12:36.834
Even after admitting
what was really going on here,

00:12:36.834 --> 00:12:38.901
Gaetz still voted with
his fellow Republicans

00:12:38.901 --> 00:12:40.400
today to remove Omar.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.434
He didn't even have the courage
to vote no on the resolution,

00:12:42.434 --> 00:12:44.501
even though he apparently had
the courage to wear this suit.

00:12:44.501 --> 00:12:45.767
I mean, look at that.

00:12:45.767 --> 00:12:47.834
Looks like a bad guy
from a futuristic videogame

00:12:47.834 --> 00:12:51.133
called "Disco Crime 3000".

00:12:51.133 --> 00:12:53.534
Republicans are censoring books
in schools,

00:12:53.534 --> 00:12:56.334
removing people from committees
whose opinions they don't like,

00:12:56.334 --> 00:12:58.968
and yet they're the ones
whining about cancel culture.

00:12:58.968 --> 00:13:01.734
The right is fully in favor of
censorship when it suits them.

00:13:01.734 --> 00:13:04.000
There's only one day a year
when Republicans can say

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.767
they're defenders
of free speech, and that's...

00:13:05.767 --> 00:13:07.300
-April Fools' Day.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.834
-This been a closer look,
everybody.

00:13:08.834 --> 00:13:12.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

